{
  "title": "Re-enable standalone Maven goal caching after output restoration is fixed",
  "description": "maven-build-cache-extension 1.3.0 enables caching standalone goals. \
After compiling Mage.Server, mvn -pl Mage.Server dependency:build-classpath removes Mage.Server/target/classes and subsequent server launch fails with ClassNotFoundException: mage.server.Main. \
Reproduced while investigating PR #1549. \
CacheControllerImpl.stagePreExistingArtifacts moves classes into root target/maven-build-cache-extension; restoreStagedArtifacts discards the staged subtree when its parent module directory already exists. \
The repository disables cacheSingleGoal in .mvn/jvm.config while keeping lifecycle caching enabled. \
Upgrade to an upstream fix and verify repeated classpath queries and resource goals preserve all compiled classes before removing that property.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "dependencies",
  ],
